From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:34:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(api): security headers, strict CORS and per-address
 rate limits [T-0142]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What changed:
- apps/api/src/security/security.ts: every API response now sends Cache-Control no-store,
  CSP "default-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'", nosniff, X-Frame-Options DENY,
  Referrer-Policy no-referrer and CORP same-origin. It also sends HSTS (max-age one year) when
  the public URL is https. X-Powered-By is removed, and trust proxy is set to a whole number of
  hops (never true).
- apps/api/src/security/rate-limit.ts: fixed-window limits per (class, client address), built
  in-house, applied before routing. Classes are auth (OIDC login/callback/step-up), webhook and
  mutating (all other POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE). An over-limit request gets 429
  {error:'rate_limited'} with Retry-After. Paths are normalised so case and trailing-slash
  variants cannot slip out of their class. The key map is bounded (oldest key evicted).
- config.ts: in production the limits are always on (auth 30, mutating 300, webhook 600 per
  60 s). LF_TRUST_PROXY_HOPS must be 0-5 (default 0); HSTS is on for an https LF_PUBLIC_URL.
- compose passes LF_TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=${LF_TRUST_PROXY_HOPS:-1} to api; install.md explains
  when to set it to 2.
- Card T-0142 set to verifying; HANDOVER now lists the ADR-0054 human gate.

Why: design §6.9 and apps/api AGENTS.md require security headers, strict CORS and rate limits.
RQ-0141 has the OWASP sources and the Express proxy semantics. ADR-0054 (security) is Proposed
and awaits the owner. No new runtime dependency.

Validation:
- RED was captured before implementation (.agent/evidence/T-0097/red-*.txt): 19 unit, 12 DB
  and 1 infra assertion failures.
- GREEN: unit 32/32, DB 17/17, infra contract 27/27 (pnpm exec vitest run infra/test).
- Regression: vitest unit+api-unit 916/916 (75 files) and api-db 223/223 (30 files), 0 skipped.
- pnpm typecheck, pnpm lint and prettier --check all clean; verify.sh --quick gate 1 PASS
  (the remaining quick gates did not finish within 10 minutes).
- One unit test's setup was corrected: both windows now open together. The asserted 8 s is
  unchanged.
- Not run: the full verify.sh, docker compose and DAST (no Docker locally, DL-0007).

Next action: run verify.sh; get codex cross-review; the owner decides on ADR-0054. Then T-0143
(backup and restore drill, RQ-0142) and T-0144 (CSRF).

